{
  "name": "Summarize merged DocupletionForms PDFs with AI and chat to ask questions later",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## AI Document Intelligence for DocupletionForms\n\n![Workflow overview](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/alfa-intellitech/n8n-nodes-docupletionforms/main/templates/images/ai-document-intelligence-assistant.png)\n\n**Uses the verified [n8n-nodes-docupletionforms](https://www.npmjs.com/package/n8n-nodes-docupletionforms) node — available on n8n Cloud and self-hosted instances.**\n\n### Who's it for\nTeams using [DocupletionForms](https://docupletionforms.com) who generate a lot of merged documents (contracts, intake packets, filings) and want an AI layer on top: an automatic summary the moment a document is ready, that summary routed to the tools the team already works in, and the ability to ask questions about any past document later without opening the PDF.\n\n### How it works\nThe DocupletionForms Trigger fires the *Document Merged* event whenever a submission is merged into a PDF for a chosen document set. The PDF is downloaded, its text extracted, and an AI chain summarizes it and pulls out a category and key points as structured data. The summary is posted to Slack, logged as a new page in a Notion database, and the original PDF is archived to Google Drive — all in the same run. The extracted text is also stored in a vector index, so a second, chat-triggered AI agent can answer natural-language questions about any document processed this way (\"what was the settlement amount on the Smith filing?\").\n\n### How to set up\n1. Add your DocupletionForms API credential and pick the Document Set to watch on the trigger.\n2. Add your OpenAI credential to both OpenAI Chat Model nodes and both Embeddings nodes (four total).\n3. Add your Slack credential and channel, your Notion credential and database (with matching \"Category\" and \"Summary\" text properties), and your Google Drive credential/folder.\n4. Optional: open the chat panel on \"Ask About Documents\" to test Q&A once at least one document has been processed.\n\n### Requirements\n- n8n (Cloud or self-hosted) with `n8n-nodes-docupletionforms` installed — on Cloud, enable it under Settings → Community Nodes; verified nodes are approved for Cloud installs.\n- A DocupletionForms account and API key.\n- An OpenAI API key (or swap in another supported n8n Chat Model / Embeddings provider).\n- Slack, Notion, and Google Drive accounts connected via their respective credentials.\n\n### How to customize\nThe in-memory vector store is the simplest way to try this out, but it only persists while your n8n instance keeps running and isn't shared across multiple workers — swap both \"Vector Store\" nodes for Pinecone, Supabase, or Qdrant for anything production-grade. Drop any of the three fan-out branches (Slack/Notion/Drive) you don't need, or add more — the summarized output is just JSON (`summary`, `category`, `key_points`) that any node can consume.",
        "height": 1160,
        "width": 660,
        "color": 1
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
